Package: delightkitr
Title: Small, Purposeless Decorative Flourishes for Web, Reports, and LaTeX
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "Brocker", email = "davidabrocker@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Claude", role = "ctb", comment = "Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 5; implementation, testing, and documentation assistance")
    )
Description: Provides "delighters" -- small decorative flourishes with no
    functional purpose, in the tradition of modelmaking greebles -- across
    three output surfaces: interactive HTML/JS/CSS widgets for Quarto HTML
    documents, Shiny apps, and standalone pages; static SVG appliques and
    borders (via grid::xsplineGrob()) for Quarto PDF/Word reports and
    ggplot2 figures; and TikZ decorations for LaTeX documents. Each surface
    has its own implementation, but they share one visual language:
    heritable, mutating traits (color drift, a smooth-to-faceted blend)
    rather than pure randomness, so a decoration never looks arbitrary.
